  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1258 AM CDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nDrier & Cooler Today, Frost Potential Tonight:\n\nNorthwesterly winds behind yesterdays cold front has begun to usher \nin a much cooler and drier airmass into the Upper Mississippi \nValley. A stout surface high pressure over the Northern Plains is \nexpected to sink southeast into the Upper Midwest through the day \ntomorrow keeping skies clear and temperatures steady in the low 60s. \nBecause of the drier airmass and light winds from the high pressure \noverhead, radiational cooling conditions will be primed Friday night \ninto Saturday morning. It's very possible that locations across \nCentral/North Central Wisconsin, and especially in the Cranberry \nBogs, could see temperatures dip near freezing and see some frost \ndevelopment overnight into Saturday. \n\nLow Rain Chances Saturday Night:\n\nA longwave trough is expected to move through the Canadian Plains \nlate Saturday into Sunday with a surface low well to our north. A \ntrailing cold front will move through our area around the same time \nand their may be enough low level convergence and moisture return to \ncreate some scattered showers for areas along and north of the I-94 \ncorridor between 00-12Z Sunday. This will be a quick hitter and most \nlocations will likely stay dry. \n\nGradual Warming & Dry Through Start Of New Week:\n\nRain chances virtually disappear from the forecast Sunday and beyond \nas yet another surface high pressure moves into the region to start \noff the work week. The pattern will be pretty similar overall with \nclear skies and temperatures in the low to mid 60s by Monday with \nsome chances for frost on Monday morning as morning lows will be in \nthe mid 30s for portions of Central and North Central Wisconsin. \nTemperatures will start to warm into mid week with highs by \nWednesday potentially reaching the 70 degree mark once again. There \nis potential for yet another trailing cold front from a surface low \nwell to our north but confidence in this system is pretty low this \nfar out and forecasts currently keep our area dry so will continue \nwith the dry and above normal blended forecast.",
